 "sentences": [
  "Using Linux will provide you with a powerful and flexible development environment.",
  "We'll work together to define the goals and scope of each sprint, typically lasting around two weeks.",
  "It keeps the team aligned and ensures we're constantly delivering value.",
  "We'll get you and your team trained up on the specifics of Scrum, and we can fine-tune the process as we go.",
  "Remember, agile is all about embracing change, so we can always adapt and improve our approach.",
  "While they can be useful in some cases, they can also cause issues and complicate things.",
  "Also, I want you to start following a specific naming convention for your functions and methods.",
  "For functions, end the name with '_fn'.",
  "And for methods, always end the name with '_ud'.",
  "These conventions will help keep your code clear and consistent with the rest of the team's.",
  "Going forward, I want you to end all method names with '_o'.",
  "This is a slight change, but it's important for consistency and readability.",
  "It's a style choice that helps us maintain a unique and recognizable pattern within our code base.",
  "It also prevents naming conflicts and makes our code more readable, especially when working with a large team.",
  "Consistency is key, and it'll make collaboration within the team smoother.",
  "But going forward, I want you to start using a Windows laptop as your main machine.",
  "Now, along with that, I want you to focus on a few specific coding practices.",
  "First, always add the @trace_class decorator from the pedantic module to all your classes."
 ],
